  "description": "An alternate to 2025-resilience, not a later layer. The thesis reference for a year's yield is the mean of ten observations that includes the year itself, so a very bad year lowers its own reference and its ratio is closer to 1 than it should be. This release uses a reference made from the 20 other observations nearest in time. Everything else is as in 2025-resilience. Australia's 100-year factor falls from 0.456 to 0.415 and the long-term capacity by about 9% (the states by 7% to 10%); the short term is unchanged.",
